# An image of galaxies (#). Every row and column with no galaxy is really
# `older` times as big.
# Part 1: the sum of the distances between every pair of galaxies, with
#         empty rows and columns doubled.
# Part 2: the same, with each empty row and column a million times as big.

example """
...#......
.......#..
#.........
..........
......#...
.#........
.........#
..........
.......#..
#...#.....
"""
  part1 = 374

example """
...#......
.......#..
#.........
..........
......#...
.#........
.........#
..........
.......#..
#...#.....
"""
  with older = 10
  part2 = 1030

example """
...#......
.......#..
#.........
